  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat is the price of a movie ticket on the last Friday? Colby's parents give him $155 each month to spend at the movies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Assuming Colby spends his entire monthly allowance on **one movie ticket each Friday**, and the month has **5 Fridays**:\n\n\\[\n\\$155 \\div 5 = \\$31\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the movie ticket on the last Friday costs\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$31}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Colby's parents give him $150 each month to spend at the movies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "If Colby spends his monthly movie allowance equally over **5 Fridays**, then:\n\n\\[\n150 \\div 5 = 30\n\\]\n\nSo, the movie ticket on the last Friday costs:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$30}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Tickets for movies on Fridays and Saturdays cost $11, while tickets on all other days cost $7.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since the last Friday is a **Friday**, its ticket costs the Friday price:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$11}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Tickets for movies on Fridays and Saturdays cost $10, while tickets on all other days cost $7.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Tickets on Fridays cost $10, so the movie ticket on the last Friday costs\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: the last Friday is a regular Friday, not a holiday or special event.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Because the last Friday is a regular Friday, the Friday ticket price applies:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Colby buys his ticket at the standard box-office price.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The standard box-office price for a regular Friday is $10. Therefore, the ticket costs\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Thanks, that helps. Now I want to figure out: How many additional movies can Colby see on the last Friday while staying within his monthly movie budget? By the way, here are some relevant details: A tub of popcorn costs $8, and a box of candy costs $2. Colby has already seen 5 movies on Fridays or Saturdays and 8 movies on other days during the month. Colby has already had 2 tubs of popcorn and 4 boxes of candy during the month, and he wants one tub of popcorn and one box of candy on the last Friday.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Calculate Colby’s spending so far:\n\n- Friday/Saturday movies: \\(\\;5 \\times \\$10 = \\$50\\)\n- Other movies: \\(\\;8 \\times \\$7 = \\$56\\)\n- Popcorn: \\(\\;2 \\times \\$8 = \\$16\\)\n- Candy: \\(\\;4 \\times \\$2 = \\$8\\)\n\nSo far, he has spent:\n\n\\[\n50+56+16+8=\\$130\n\\]\n\nOn the last Friday, he plans to spend:\n\n\\[\n\\$10+\\$8+\\$2=\\$20\n\\]\n\nThis uses his entire budget:\n\n\\[\n130+20=150\n\\]\n\nTherefore, he has no money left for additional movie tickets:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
